ROLE: product_realist  VOTE: yellow
REAL_USE_CASE: Teams training multilingual LLMs on web-crawl corpora (C4/OSCAR/FineWeb) where the model tokenizer applies NFKC+casefold (e.g., SentencePiece, Arnett2025-style) but the dedup pipeline runs raw/NFC/NFD. Model-identical pairs differing only by compatibility equivalence (fullwidth↔halfwidth, ligatures, case variants, precomposed↔combining) escape the deduper, inflating duplicate training, memorization, and privacy-contamination risk that is invisible to dedup metrics.
OPERATIONAL_SIGNIFICANCE: Real win for multilingual regimes with compatibility variants; microbench-only for ASCII-centric or already-aggressively-normalized pipelines. L0 EXP-0068 shows FN=1.00 (total miss) under raw/NFC vs 0.00 after NFKC+casefold alignment, reproduced over 7 seeds (±0.00) and flat across T=[0.5,0.9]. Synthetic corpus overstates prevalence; packet provides no real-world rate of normalizable pairs in production corpora. Datatrove’s NFD diacritic-stripping (src/datatrove/utils/text.py:254-255) does not collapse NFKC compatibility classes, so the seam remains open for fullwidth/ligature/casefold pairs.
ADOPTION_BARRIER: [Tooling lacks model-aware normalization knob: datatrove TextNormConfig (src/datatrove/utils/text.py:186-196) offers lowercase/NFD/punct-removal but no NFKC or casefold option; NeMo Curator fuzzy dedup contains no unicode normalization (grep of /tmp/curator/nemo_curator/stages/deduplication/fuzzy/*.py returns null); text-dedup preprocess.py (line 35) only lowercases. Cross-team config split: tokenizer normalization lives in model-training repo, dedup normalization lives in data-pipeline repo; no shared config surface or co-location mechanism observed. Detection is invisible: dedup recall metrics appear healthy while the model sees duplicates; no production telemetry surfaces the divergence. Risk of semantic drift if operators apply NFKC blindly without understanding model-specific equivalence classes.]
RATIONALE: Packet L0 demonstrates the coupling is upstream of LSH (Jaccard collapses to ~0 under weak normalizer, Table “frac J≥0.8 (raw)” = 0.000), and the alias control (typo arm) confirms divergence—not edit distance—drives FN. Prior-art search via TOOLING_v001.md (web_search, gh, repo clone) finds zero evidence that datatrove, NeMo Curator, text-dedup, or BigCode pipelines expose a “model-normalizer-alignment” mode; all default to fixed internal normalization. This satisfies the CLAIM-0058 stress-test: the seam is genuinely open in deployed practice. ORG-SEAM (independent team configs) is assumed, not demonstrated, in the packet—insufficient evidence for organizational claim. Operational significance is regime-dependent: the 1.00→0.00 swing is not a microbenchmark artifact, but the product value scales with the (unmeasured) fraction of compatibility-variant pairs in a given corpus. For English-centric data the win is negligible; for multilingual web crawl it is material. Honest YELLOW reflects a valid, narrow coupling with actionable guidance (align normalizers) but limited universal product impact.
